/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`) is the primary contributor/agent on-ramp for\nthe Gerrit LLM-Review gate — AGENTS.md points at it directly. Ticket bb9b landed the\ncontributor-triggerable re-review (comment `recheck-review` on a change; merged as Gerrit\nchange 1243, live in production), and docs/review-policy.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and the\nreview-bot runbook were updated with it — but the packaged guide was missed: lines\n112–114 still tell the contributor a coverage-gap BLOCK requires \"a maintainer\nre-triggers; re-pushing the same commit or pinging the maintainer is the move\". That is\nnow wrong (self-service exists) and it is the single most discoverable surface, so the\nstale text actively misdirects contributors to ping maintainers.\n\n## What\n\nUpdate `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`'s coverage-gap bullet (§\"Reading the\nvote\", lines ~112–114) to say: a coverage-gap `-1` is an infrastructure veto, not your\ndiff — once the infra issue clears, comment **`recheck-review`** on the change to\nre-trigger the review yourself (the bot refuses only when the standing `-1` is a real\nfinding); mention that `recheck` (CI) and `recheck-review` (LLM review) mirror each\nother, consistent with CONTRIBUTING.md §2c and docs/review-policy.md. Keep the guide's\nexisting tone and line-wrap discipline. Doc-only change: no code, no tests to add;\nvalidation is `make lint` (format/whitespace) and grepping the rendered guide via\n`rebar explain review` in the worktree venv.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` coverage-gap bullet names `recheck-review` as the contributor self-service re-trigger and no longer instructs pinging a maintainer as the primary move.\n- [ ] AC2: The change is merged via Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, carrying the rebar-ticket trailer.\n- [ ] AC3: `rebar explain review` run from the updated worktree shows the new text (packaged guide ships from source, no build step needed).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md","reason":"coverage-gap bullet updated to name the recheck-review self-service trigger"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2b66-2a43-6d0c-472b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"dece98a3-ebb1-4c83-afc1-d37201aaf6fa","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f418-1b22-43f0-47ff","ticket_type":"task","title":"Update packaged code-review guide for recheck-review","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["56bb0cb1-670d-4f10-856c-fe61f632ed1a","5403ea49-ad42-4693-b026-9c2be6fa84ef","add926a8-553b-4675-be00-1853a46ab807","b05fc100-f4b2-467e-af7f-3b8ced9a96c6","0be86dad-2ba3-4b41-b204-9d034a4567fc","dece98a3-ebb1-4c83-afc1-d37201aaf6fa","bbd07351-fc90-4328-a061-00daec90fce9","f7ffcdaa-19b3-436b-999d-eb0c29b0c63d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785725117894534587,"uuid":"09fb4aa4-9b4d-4b86-8da4-28589cb95d57"}